Semileptonic transitions involving the decay of doubly charmed baryons into single leptons and corresponding hadrons are examined within the framework of the Pochhut model. The study calculates relevant form factors for the vector, axial, and pseudoscalar currents, utilizing these theoretical results to analyze the decay rates and kinematic distributions of specific processes: $\Xi_{cc}^{\pm}	o\Xi^{\pm}\ell^{+}
u_{\ell}$, $\Omega_{cc}^{\pm}	o\Sigma^{\pm}\ell^{+}
u_{\ell}$, and $\Xi_{cc}^{\pm}	o\Xi^{\pm}\ell^{+}
u_{\ell}$.
